.TH okf-jawn-mcp 1  "mcp " 
.SH NAME
okf\-jawn\-mcp \- Relay MCP messages between a local client\*(Aqs standard streams and the running service, starting the local service when none is running
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBokf\-jawn mcp\fR [\fB\-\-server\fR] [\fB\-\-token\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-server\-bin\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-stdio\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Relay MCP messages between a local client\*(Aqs standard streams and the running service, starting the local service when none is running
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-server\fR \fI<URL>\fR [default: http://127.0.0.1:7711]
The service address: HTTPS, or HTTP for a loopback address
.TP
\fB\-\-stdio\fR
Speak MCP over standard input and output, one JSON\-RPC message per line
.TP
\fB\-\-token\-file\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Read the connector credential from the first line of this file
.TP
\fB\-\-server\-bin\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
The server executable to start when no local service is running (default: okf\-jawn\-server beside this executable)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH EXTRA
The connector credential is read from the OKF_JAWN_TOKEN environment variable, or from the first line of the file named by \-\-token\-file. It is never an argument.
